                                                "sense_id": "9f65c6cd-9747-3677-8899-871302b6d27d",
                                                "text": "Or it may be that the trains continue to pass but never more will stop, and the platforms are stripped and laid bare, the doorways bricked up, the overbridges dismantled, and the empty buildings stare out upon the passing trains with the reproachful melancholy of an old tombstone in a city churchyard overlooking a city street."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20904ec5-6278-3390-8fcf-49e23b67f2bd",
                                        "entry_id": "a2dfa7b5-1f79-36d8-ac39-d1af80604209",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To trap or seal in a closed space using bricks."
